# C2: mlmf-source-file's direct dependencies. Changing this file is a
# deliberate act. Keep sorted -- `deps.rs::direct_dependencies_match_allowlist`
# compares against the manifest's sorted dependency list with `assert_eq!`
# over a VECTOR, not a set, so an entry in the wrong position fails exactly
# as a missing one does.
#
# `memmap2` is FIRST because the comparison is positional: the manifest's
# dependency list is sorted before the assert, and `memmap2` sorts before
# `mlmf-core` (`me` < `ml`). Written below `mlmf-core` in `Cargo.toml`, where
# it reads better beside the `[features]` table it exists for, and above it
# here, where the order is the assertion. An entry in the wrong position
# fails exactly as a missing one does.
#
# It is an OPTIONAL dependency and it is still an edge: `parse_manifest`
# takes every name in `[dependencies]` regardless of `optional`, which is
# right -- a default feature makes this edge the one every consumer gets
# unless they ask otherwise, and C2 pins edges rather than the subset of them
# somebody happens to compile.
memmap2

# Spec §3.1 is why mlmf-core is the only entry this crate may ever have on
# the FORMAT side: "sources depend on mlmf-core only, never on a format
# crate". An edge to mlmf-gguf or mlmf-safetensors here would make this
# source usable with one format, which is the composition the two-axis
# design exists to avoid needing.
mlmf-core
